1
00:00:00,172 --> 00:00:02,414
If you tell me
that you don't have feelings for Thear,

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:04,875
I'll let you stay here.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,390
I think I'm in love
with Inspector Thear.

4
00:00:06,415 --> 00:00:08,102
Then take him back!

5
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:10,555
Stop acting
like you're his second choice.

6
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:11,664
What you're doing

7
00:00:11,689 --> 00:00:13,226
makes it seem like
you don't care about him at all.

8
00:00:13,251 --> 00:00:15,773
Yet you have heeded none of my words.

9
00:00:15,798 --> 00:00:18,164
The heaven and earth
do not acknowledge your love.

10
00:00:18,195 --> 00:00:20,438
Please just let me
be a good husband for once.

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,025
Hey, Mungkorn!

12
00:00:27,834 --> 00:00:29,288
Whoa, that was a close call.

13
00:00:43,052 --> 00:00:45,787
I'm begging you.
Please tell me how to fix this.

14
00:00:46,052 --> 00:00:49,489
Mungkorn shall take your misfortune
upon himself

15
00:00:50,552 --> 00:00:56,123
until the day one of you betrays the vow
or ends the marriage.

16
00:00:56,857 --> 00:00:57,841
When that time comes,

17
00:00:58,388 --> 00:01:03,177
the scales of fate will gradually return
to their former balance.

18
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:08,615
Hello, Belle?

19
00:01:10,763 --> 00:01:12,123
I need your help with something.

20
00:01:12,701 --> 00:01:13,661
Inspector.

21
00:01:13,971 --> 00:01:15,351
So, what's going on here?

22
00:01:15,435 --> 00:01:17,802
We'll just have to wait and see.

23
00:01:18,943 --> 00:01:20,771
Next time, I hope
you realize your feelings sooner

24
00:01:20,796 --> 00:01:22,371
so that you won't waste anyone's time.

25
00:01:33,474 --> 00:01:35,234
(I'll do whatever it takes,)

26
00:01:35,784 --> 00:01:37,794
(to keep you safe, Mungkorn.)

27
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,700
Wait, Inspector.

28
00:01:48,172 --> 00:01:49,622
No more waiting.

29
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,160
Please just let me
be a good husband for once.

30
00:02:01,542 --> 00:02:02,472
Hey, Mungkorn!

31
00:02:08,261 --> 00:02:09,401
Are you hurt? Did it hit you?

32
00:02:10,248 --> 00:02:11,128
I'm okay.

33
00:02:11,781 --> 00:02:13,201
Whoa, that was a close call.

34
00:02:27,651 --> 00:02:29,013
What were you thinking?
You scared the life out of me.

35
00:02:29,037 --> 00:02:31,081
What if you fell and hit your head?

36
00:02:31,225 --> 00:02:32,243
I'm sorry.

37
00:02:32,728 --> 00:02:36,043
It's hot, so I brought you your favorite

38
00:02:36,494 --> 00:02:37,705
to keep you cool and refreshed.

39
00:02:44,351 --> 00:02:46,043
Thear, when you came to work,

40
00:02:46,456 --> 00:02:47,858
you didn't wait for me at all.

41
00:02:49,901 --> 00:02:51,508
I was in a rush.

42
00:02:54,061 --> 00:02:55,001
That's okay.

43
00:02:56,108 --> 00:02:57,551
I just missed you.

44
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:02,133
I missed the time we spent in the tent

45
00:03:03,049 --> 00:03:05,262
when we held each other...

46
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,988
when we kissed...

47
00:03:12,019 --> 00:03:14,062
and when we...

48
00:03:16,337 --> 00:03:19,071
I told you not to act like this at work.

49
00:03:19,102 --> 00:03:20,761
What if people see us?

50
00:03:20,786 --> 00:03:22,683
Come on, they won't.

51
00:03:23,043 --> 00:03:26,028
I've already checked, Hubby.

52
00:03:27,274 --> 00:03:29,938
I'm begging you.
Please don't call me that.

53
00:03:32,155 --> 00:03:33,184
Get to work.

54
00:03:48,845 --> 00:03:51,871
We need to gather as much intel
on the Black Bull as possible.

55
00:03:52,875 --> 00:03:54,688
We've only caught the small fry.

56
00:03:55,482 --> 00:03:57,548
We still haven't traced it back
to the boss yet.

57
00:03:58,307 --> 00:03:59,282
Understood.

58
00:03:59,307 --> 00:04:01,778
I'll make sure
to squeeze some solid info out of them.

59
00:04:02,235 --> 00:04:03,078
It's fine.

60
00:04:04,075 --> 00:04:05,345
I have someone coming to help.

61
00:04:06,381 --> 00:04:09,385
The department sent an expert
from Phayao Station.

62
00:04:10,141 --> 00:04:10,975
Who is it?

63
00:04:28,025 --> 00:04:29,603
This is Police Major Saming.

64
00:04:29,945 --> 00:04:32,098
He volunteered to help us himself.

65
00:04:32,774 --> 00:04:34,041
We already know each other quite well.

66
00:04:35,953 --> 00:04:37,920
But we've been working just fine
on our own.

67
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:39,626
I don't see any reason
to bring in outside help.

68
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:41,483
Come on, just work together.

69
00:04:41,741 --> 00:04:44,568
Saming has been handling
this case in Phayao for some time now.

70
00:04:44,888 --> 00:04:47,091
He knows them inside out.

71
00:04:48,115 --> 00:04:50,401
The Black Bull won't stand a chance.

72
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:12,634
(Yin as Theartha)

73
00:05:17,431 --> 00:05:20,145
(War as Mungkorn)

74
00:05:24,185 --> 00:05:26,478
(Shane as Phuwin)

75
00:05:27,098 --> 00:05:29,985
(Boss as Lukplub)

76
00:05:32,338 --> 00:05:34,191
(Kit as Kanin)

77
00:05:34,545 --> 00:05:36,291
(Tang as Nadol)

78
00:05:38,498 --> 00:05:43,258
(Tae as Saming)

79
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:21,296
Whoa, Captains.

80
00:06:21,651 --> 00:06:23,243
Why are you looking so sharp?

81
00:06:23,377 --> 00:06:24,386
Where are you headed?

82
00:06:24,411 --> 00:06:26,323
We're going to a karaoke bar in San Sai.

83
00:06:26,347 --> 00:06:29,124
An informant says
another drug deal is going down today.

84
00:06:29,149 --> 00:06:31,317
We suspect it's the Black Bull again.

85
00:06:31,995 --> 00:06:33,985
These bastards
are like a never-ending plague.

86
00:06:34,010 --> 00:06:36,171
I'm dying to know who the boss is.

87
00:06:36,209 --> 00:06:37,698
Bet he's a real piece of work.

88
00:06:37,962 --> 00:06:39,582
Please let me come along.

89
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,467
I've got plenty of intel
to take them down.

90
00:06:43,065 --> 00:06:44,243
Count yourself in.

91
00:06:44,856 --> 00:06:46,358
I wasn't thrilled
about going with just him anyway.

92
00:06:46,383 --> 00:06:49,278
Hey, if it's just us,
we can pose as a couple.

93
00:06:50,308 --> 00:06:52,713
Is that really necessary?
We could just be friends.

94
00:06:52,738 --> 00:06:54,097
A couple is a much better cover.

95
00:06:55,065 --> 00:06:56,723
I think we should let him join us.

96
00:06:56,747 --> 00:06:59,065
I heard they've got quite a few guys.

97
00:06:59,508 --> 00:07:02,205
Alright. I'll go change, then.

98
00:07:04,708 --> 00:07:07,185
Sergeant Mungkorn, where are you going?

99
00:07:08,067 --> 00:07:10,907
To help Captains arrest the Black Bull
at a karaoke bar.

100
00:07:11,201 --> 00:07:11,963
You can't go.

101
00:07:12,414 --> 00:07:15,225
Why would you go?
You're not assigned to this mission.

102
00:07:15,754 --> 00:07:17,487
But I have all the intel on them.

103
00:07:17,774 --> 00:07:19,203
But it's not your job.

104
00:07:19,437 --> 00:07:20,828
Let those two handle it.

105
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,563
Please let me go.

106
00:07:24,930 --> 00:07:27,384
Besides, I've already finished
all the paperwork I was assigned.

107
00:07:27,409 --> 00:07:28,283
I said no.

108
00:07:28,445 --> 00:07:29,803
Did you not understand?

109
00:07:29,828 --> 00:07:31,403
When I give you an order,
you follow it.

110
00:07:31,531 --> 00:07:32,858
I'm your superior.

111
00:07:41,194 --> 00:07:42,698
I understand you're my superior,

112
00:07:44,191 --> 00:07:46,445
but a superior who just barks orders
whenever he feels like it

113
00:07:47,247 --> 00:07:48,113
and does whatever he wants

114
00:07:48,137 --> 00:07:50,798
without any regard for his subordinates,

115
00:07:51,875 --> 00:07:53,427
I don't consider that a good leader.

116
00:07:53,452 --> 00:07:55,065
You have no right to talk back to me.

117
00:08:02,254 --> 00:08:03,147
Yes, sir.

118
00:08:05,051 --> 00:08:06,678
Then I'll just keep my mouth shut

119
00:08:07,607 --> 00:08:09,674
and follow every single one
of your orders.

120
00:08:11,575 --> 00:08:12,848
Just tell me where to walk,

121
00:08:13,375 --> 00:08:14,288
what to do,

122
00:08:14,874 --> 00:08:16,268
or what to say.

123
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:18,671
That way, I'll know how to behave.

124
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:30,525
Hey, take it easy.

125
00:08:30,926 --> 00:08:32,481
Why are you so worked up?

126
00:08:33,274 --> 00:08:35,188
I think Mungkorn just wanted to help.

127
00:08:35,701 --> 00:08:38,523
I get it, but it's not his job.

128
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:41,585
What if something happens to him?

129
00:09:15,071 --> 00:09:17,443
I'll go back to my table for now.

130
00:09:17,896 --> 00:09:19,141
Be back in a bit.

131
00:09:24,908 --> 00:09:26,043
Mungkorn,

132
00:09:26,532 --> 00:09:28,090
why are you downing it neat like that?

133
00:09:35,541 --> 00:09:36,763
Don't tell me...

134
00:09:37,297 --> 00:09:38,723
that Inspector Thear...

135
00:09:40,041 --> 00:09:41,778
Don't mention that name, please.

136
00:09:42,821 --> 00:09:45,918
He's terrified
that people might get the wrong idea.

137
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:47,298
Jeez.

138
00:09:49,428 --> 00:09:50,323
I knew it.

139
00:09:50,952 --> 00:09:51,950
I had a feeling.

140
00:09:52,271 --> 00:09:54,363
My intuition is really sharp, you know.

141
00:09:54,503 --> 00:09:58,187
I could tell from the start
who was the top and who was the bottom.

142
00:09:59,151 --> 00:10:01,819
There's no such thing
as top or bottom anymore.

143
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:05,605
All that's left is a disaster
from top to bottom.

144
00:10:08,305 --> 00:10:10,883
So, why don't you tell me...

145
00:10:11,374 --> 00:10:12,797
what he did?

146
00:10:13,168 --> 00:10:15,163
I promise you that...

147
00:10:15,707 --> 00:10:19,114
I'll take this secret to my grave.

148
00:10:19,295 --> 00:10:21,225
He did everything.

149
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:24,281
He just didn't mean any of it.

150
00:10:25,801 --> 00:10:27,471
I was so stupid,

151
00:10:27,496 --> 00:10:29,650
deluding myself,

152
00:10:29,675 --> 00:10:31,278
thinking that someone like me

153
00:10:32,167 --> 00:10:34,418
could actually make
an inspector fall in love.

154
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,052
Mao.

155
00:10:46,203 --> 00:10:46,723
Yes?

156
00:10:46,748 --> 00:10:48,091
Has Mungkorn not come back yet?

157
00:10:48,116 --> 00:10:49,265
I haven't seen him.

158
00:10:56,028 --> 00:10:57,163
What happened?

159
00:10:57,187 --> 00:10:58,778
Why isn't he home yet?

160
00:11:00,132 --> 00:11:01,310
I think...

161
00:11:02,383 --> 00:11:03,920
I was too hard on him today.

162
00:11:03,945 --> 00:11:05,483
He just disappeared after I scolded him.

163
00:11:05,842 --> 00:11:08,956
I thought I'd see him when I got home,
but he's not here.

164
00:11:10,899 --> 00:11:12,975
You need to take this
more seriously, Thear.

165
00:11:13,421 --> 00:11:15,661
Either way,
Mungkorn is the one getting hurt.

166
00:11:17,841 --> 00:11:20,911
If he can't take it anymore
and doesn't come back,

167
00:11:21,334 --> 00:11:23,085
you'll regret it the most.

168
00:11:35,504 --> 00:11:37,558
Aw.

169
00:11:38,075 --> 00:11:40,978
Poor innocent little bunny,

170
00:11:41,097 --> 00:11:45,219
getting his heart crushed by a lion.

171
00:11:45,974 --> 00:11:47,214
This is what they call...

172
00:11:47,627 --> 00:11:49,936
a lesson in love.

173
00:11:49,961 --> 00:11:54,396
Next time, know your place
before falling for someone.

174
00:11:54,421 --> 00:11:57,740
Save some of your heart
to love yourself, too.

175
00:12:00,754 --> 00:12:02,961
Come on, let me pour you another glass.

176
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:07,368
Since it's sad, let's make it strong.

177
00:12:07,628 --> 00:12:09,027
I've got you covered.

178
00:12:13,554 --> 00:12:16,485
Drink this one to forget him.

179
00:12:22,708 --> 00:12:23,771
Saming?

180
00:12:25,148 --> 00:12:25,859
Oh...

181
00:12:26,771 --> 00:12:29,683
You're Police Major Saming,
the heartthrob of Phayao Station?

182
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:30,883
Hello.

183
00:12:30,908 --> 00:12:32,261
Hello. Mind if I join you?

184
00:12:32,286 --> 00:12:34,408
Not at all. Please have a seat.

185
00:12:36,341 --> 00:12:38,456
It's great that you're here, Inspector.

186
00:12:38,481 --> 00:12:42,695
I think Mungkorn could really use
someone to cheer him up tonight.

187
00:12:42,976 --> 00:12:46,563
I'll excuse myself to the bar for a bit.

188
00:12:46,734 --> 00:12:49,171
I was in the middle of hitting on a guy.

189
00:12:49,196 --> 00:12:50,248
Sure, go ahead.

190
00:12:50,273 --> 00:12:51,351
I'll leave him in your hands.

191
00:12:52,701 --> 00:12:53,781
Don't get too drunk.

192
00:12:54,475 --> 00:12:55,448
Too late.

193
00:12:55,975 --> 00:12:57,178
He's quite something.

194
00:12:57,334 --> 00:12:59,891
Barely got over a guy from Chiang Mai,
and now he's got a Phayao hottie.

195
00:13:00,148 --> 00:13:00,948
Here we go.

196
00:13:11,947 --> 00:13:13,003
That's enough.

197
00:13:13,097 --> 00:13:15,381
You won't make it home
if you get any drunker.

198
00:13:16,231 --> 00:13:18,026
Saming, just let me drink

199
00:13:19,011 --> 00:13:20,558
so I can just forget about everything.

200
00:13:29,627 --> 00:13:31,971
Why the long face, though?

201
00:13:32,941 --> 00:13:35,011
You can tell me everything, you know.

202
00:13:36,059 --> 00:13:37,712
It's nothing.

203
00:13:38,425 --> 00:13:41,336
Just a sad story about a fool.

204
00:13:42,268 --> 00:13:45,684
Anyone in love can end up being a fool.

205
00:13:46,911 --> 00:13:49,618
I know. I've been there myself.

206
00:13:53,495 --> 00:13:56,763
But I'm the biggest fool of them all.

207
00:13:58,041 --> 00:14:00,345
I knew full well
what kind of person he was.

208
00:14:02,074 --> 00:14:02,823
A smooth-talking,

209
00:14:03,007 --> 00:14:03,737
deceitful,

210
00:14:03,890 --> 00:14:05,163
shameless liar.

211
00:14:05,343 --> 00:14:06,870
And yet, I trusted him.

212
00:14:08,685 --> 00:14:11,458
I let my guard down and fell for him.

213
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:14,798
I really didn't know my place.

214
00:14:15,675 --> 00:14:18,365
I know full well
I'm just meant to ward off his bad luck.

215
00:14:19,975 --> 00:14:21,229
Ward off his bad luck?

216
00:14:21,675 --> 00:14:23,658
What do you mean by that?

217
00:14:28,559 --> 00:14:30,255
It's nothing.

218
00:14:32,175 --> 00:14:34,578
I'm just drunk and talking nonsense.

219
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:40,784
Mungkorn.

220
00:14:42,891 --> 00:14:44,031
Listen to me.

221
00:14:46,111 --> 00:14:47,403
A guy like that

222
00:14:48,119 --> 00:14:49,763
isn't worth your love.

223
00:14:51,421 --> 00:14:53,121
You deserve someone better.

224
00:14:55,095 --> 00:14:56,143
If it were me,

225
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:59,221
I would never hurt you.

226
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:03,945
I'd never let you be just a rebound

227
00:15:04,268 --> 00:15:06,475
while waiting for an ex to come back.

228
00:15:07,675 --> 00:15:08,698
Do you understand?

229
00:15:12,393 --> 00:15:13,245
Come here.

230
00:15:58,778 --> 00:16:00,556
We've been here for so long
we're almost wasted.

231
00:16:00,581 --> 00:16:02,150
Haven't those guys shown up yet?

232
00:16:02,175 --> 00:16:03,775
Let's not say "we," Captain.

233
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:06,528
You finished all five bottles yourself.

234
00:16:06,908 --> 00:16:08,661
I've only been drinking water.

235
00:16:09,594 --> 00:16:12,641
Hey, I was just staying in character.

236
00:16:12,994 --> 00:16:15,988
Sitting here all stiff and serious
would look suspicious.

237
00:16:18,074 --> 00:16:20,102
Drinking alcohol while on duty

238
00:16:20,295 --> 00:16:23,071
will impair your performance
and decision-making.

239
00:16:23,974 --> 00:16:25,061
You're always reciting the rules.

240
00:16:25,508 --> 00:16:27,588
Have you ever had any fun in your life?

241
00:16:28,193 --> 00:16:30,087
Learn to let loose, will you?

242
00:16:39,108 --> 00:16:40,211
What are you doing?

243
00:16:41,568 --> 00:16:42,434
Tell you what.

244
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:46,655
I promise
I'll speak nicely to you from now on.

245
00:16:47,738 --> 00:16:51,043
I only tease you
because when you're mad,

246
00:16:51,676 --> 00:16:52,930
it's cute.

247
00:16:56,328 --> 00:16:59,124
But I really want to
punch you right now.

248
00:17:00,301 --> 00:17:01,323
You want to punch me?

249
00:17:01,954 --> 00:17:04,344
Do it. Go on, punch me.

250
00:17:05,021 --> 00:17:05,843
No, Captain.

251
00:17:05,867 --> 00:17:07,676
We're on duty.

252
00:17:07,701 --> 00:17:08,936
Captain, stop.

253
00:17:10,721 --> 00:17:11,963
If you don't punch me,

254
00:17:12,704 --> 00:17:13,804
I'm going to kiss you.

255
00:17:15,435 --> 00:17:16,400
Captain...

256
00:17:46,681 --> 00:17:49,448
Well, well, well.

257
00:17:49,982 --> 00:17:51,261
Officers,

258
00:17:51,874 --> 00:17:53,507
you're here to arrest us, aren't you?

259
00:17:54,285 --> 00:17:57,022
Why are you being so lovey-dovey?

260
00:17:57,508 --> 00:17:58,818
Wow.

261
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,820
Can we really handle this, Captain?

262
00:18:03,831 --> 00:18:05,016
Are you ready?

263
00:18:06,890 --> 00:18:08,396
I guess I am.

264
00:18:08,708 --> 00:18:09,683
I was asking...

265
00:18:10,048 --> 00:18:10,929
if you were ready to run.

266
00:18:10,954 --> 00:18:11,968
Where do you think you're going?

267
00:18:27,595 --> 00:18:28,602
Go, go, go!

268
00:18:30,782 --> 00:18:31,683
After them!

269
00:18:42,632 --> 00:18:43,965
We're sorry.

270
00:18:44,461 --> 00:18:45,344
Mungkorn,

271
00:18:46,118 --> 00:18:47,271
are you okay?

272
00:18:47,612 --> 00:18:48,692
I'm sorry, Saming.

273
00:18:52,613 --> 00:18:53,403
It's alright.

274
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:55,665
Go ahead and fall.
I'm right here to catch you.

275
00:18:56,827 --> 00:19:00,311
Whoever gets to be your partner
will be the luckiest person alive.

276
00:19:00,561 --> 00:19:02,124
You take such good care of people.

277
00:19:03,032 --> 00:19:04,161
So...

278
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:07,172
don't you want to be that lucky person?

279
00:19:20,903 --> 00:19:22,358
(Po-love Officers
Nadol: The raid failed. It was a trap.)

280
00:19:25,461 --> 00:19:26,228
Mungkorn?

281
00:19:27,175 --> 00:19:28,324
Is something wrong?

282
00:19:29,355 --> 00:19:30,878
It's a message from the group chat.

283
00:19:31,578 --> 00:19:35,383
It says the raid mission failed.

284
00:19:35,408 --> 00:19:36,901
They were caught in a trap.

285
00:19:37,821 --> 00:19:39,171
Is everyone okay?

286
00:19:41,108 --> 00:19:42,895
Luckily, no one was hurt.

287
00:19:43,761 --> 00:19:45,508
The Black Bull...

288
00:19:46,128 --> 00:19:47,882
won't let themselves be caught easily.

289
00:19:48,828 --> 00:19:50,255
The only way to catch them

290
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:52,385
is if they actually want to be caught.

291
00:19:54,635 --> 00:19:55,395
Come on.

292
00:19:56,301 --> 00:19:59,031
Let's go. Time to get some sleep.
I'll give you a ride.

293
00:19:59,056 --> 00:20:01,661
It's fine. I'll go home on my own.

294
00:20:01,781 --> 00:20:03,451
No way. Not when you're this wasted.

295
00:20:03,790 --> 00:20:04,722
I'll give you a ride.

296
00:20:04,747 --> 00:20:06,211
Oh, it's really okay.

297
00:20:06,236 --> 00:20:08,041
I'll just call a cab. It's a short trip.

298
00:20:08,071 --> 00:20:10,027
No, it's dangerous.

299
00:20:10,052 --> 00:20:12,575
Look, you could even stay at my place.

300
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,268
- No, thanks. I don't want to impose.
- Come on.

301
00:20:14,293 --> 00:20:15,841
You're not imposing. Let's go.

302
00:20:16,408 --> 00:20:18,815
Let go of him. Leave him to me.

303
00:20:18,987 --> 00:20:21,120
Thear? How did you get here?

304
00:20:21,301 --> 00:20:23,803
Maybe by a chopper. Stay out of this.

305
00:20:23,948 --> 00:20:25,514
I'm giving him a ride.

306
00:20:27,048 --> 00:20:28,378
Who are you to give me orders?

307
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:31,291
And what exactly are you to him?

308
00:20:35,581 --> 00:20:36,781
Whatever, it doesn't matter,

309
00:20:36,974 --> 00:20:38,707
but he's under my responsibility.

310
00:20:38,732 --> 00:20:40,865
He's my subordinate
who reports directly to me.

311
00:20:40,941 --> 00:20:41,858
I'll take care of him.

312
00:20:48,361 --> 00:20:50,258
Do you take such good care
of all your subordinates?

313
00:20:51,908 --> 00:20:53,683
You were watching over him
when he was in the hospital,

314
00:20:53,708 --> 00:20:55,635
and now you've followed him to a bar.

315
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:00,480
This kind of behavior

316
00:21:01,248 --> 00:21:03,505
goes way beyond
that of a boss and subordinate.

317
00:21:05,075 --> 00:21:08,474
I just don't want him to be around
an untrustworthy guy like you.

318
00:21:10,961 --> 00:21:12,228
Have you even asked him

319
00:21:13,101 --> 00:21:14,768
if he wants you to take care of him?

320
00:21:22,998 --> 00:21:26,468
Did you know he was sitting here
crying his eyes out?

321
00:21:27,697 --> 00:21:28,428
Leave.

322
00:21:29,141 --> 00:21:30,785
Go back to your girl.

323
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:34,787
I'll take care of Mungkorn myself.

324
00:21:35,914 --> 00:21:37,978
Let's go and stay at my place.

325
00:21:40,651 --> 00:21:41,981
Why the hell would he go with you?

326
00:21:42,005 --> 00:21:44,095
He has a home. I'll take him there.

327
00:21:44,748 --> 00:21:46,521
But he doesn't want to go with you.

328
00:21:46,671 --> 00:21:48,241
But I'm taking him home.

329
00:21:49,187 --> 00:21:50,675
What right do you have
to tell him what to do?

330
00:21:50,841 --> 00:21:52,581
It's after work hours.

331
00:21:53,214 --> 00:21:55,039
Are you his boss or his husband?

332
00:21:58,474 --> 00:21:59,274
Come with me.

333
00:22:00,049 --> 00:22:01,605
Whatever, he's coming with me.

334
00:22:01,630 --> 00:22:04,209
- But he doesn't want to go with you.
- How would you know?

335
00:22:04,641 --> 00:22:05,950
He's going with me.

336
00:22:05,975 --> 00:22:07,250
I'm making him go with me.

337
00:22:07,275 --> 00:22:08,796
Jeez, enough already!

338
00:22:11,061 --> 00:22:12,185
I'll leave on my own.

339
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:33,137
Mungkorn!

340
00:22:33,534 --> 00:22:34,604
Hear me out.

341
00:22:35,441 --> 00:22:36,277
Listen to what I have to say.

342
00:22:36,958 --> 00:22:38,108
- Let's go home together.
- No!

343
00:22:39,101 --> 00:22:42,071
I'm not going with someone
as unpredictable as you.

344
00:22:42,911 --> 00:22:43,893
I'll go back by myself.

345
00:22:43,924 --> 00:22:46,078
How exactly? Just come with me.

346
00:22:47,175 --> 00:22:48,418
I said no!

347
00:22:48,975 --> 00:22:51,672
I don't trust a liar like you anymore.

348
00:22:54,134 --> 00:22:55,758
You want to take me home?

349
00:22:57,854 --> 00:22:59,957
Did you hit your head or something?

350
00:23:01,775 --> 00:23:03,142
Let's just talk when we get home.

351
00:23:03,387 --> 00:23:04,291
We're going home together.

352
00:23:04,575 --> 00:23:06,011
I'm not going home!

353
00:23:07,078 --> 00:23:10,130
What if you tell me to get out again?

354
00:23:10,868 --> 00:23:11,635
What am I supposed to do?

355
00:23:13,427 --> 00:23:15,685
I'm not some rich guy's plaything,
you know.

356
00:23:17,362 --> 00:23:18,857
So, you just wanted to sleep with me?

357
00:23:20,908 --> 00:23:22,378
Why are you doing this?

358
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:23,757
Say something!

359
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:26,285
If you've got something to say,
just say it!

360
00:23:27,126 --> 00:23:28,111
What the hell is wrong with you?

361
00:23:29,947 --> 00:23:30,868
Oh, hey!

362
00:23:33,314 --> 00:23:35,063
- It's me.
- Wait, hold on a second.

363
00:23:35,094 --> 00:23:37,142
He's with me. I'll give him a ride.

364
00:23:37,775 --> 00:23:39,274
He doesn't want to be with me.

365
00:23:40,641 --> 00:23:42,378
Where are you going to sleep, then?

366
00:23:45,041 --> 00:23:46,231
Anywhere,

367
00:23:46,827 --> 00:23:48,797
as long as it's not with a player.

368
00:23:49,265 --> 00:23:51,491
- Let's go.
- Wait! Please...

369
00:23:51,516 --> 00:23:52,591
Hey, Mungkorn!

370
00:24:20,948 --> 00:24:22,851
Is this your first time
handling an interrogation?

371
00:24:24,262 --> 00:24:25,538
I've actually done it before,

372
00:24:26,598 --> 00:24:28,881
but something went wrong that time.

373
00:24:30,122 --> 00:24:31,895
These guys are incredibly slippery.

374
00:24:32,654 --> 00:24:35,054
If you get a lead
during the first interrogation,

375
00:24:35,488 --> 00:24:36,755
it means they're just playing you.

376
00:24:38,275 --> 00:24:39,665
You don't need to worry.

377
00:24:41,708 --> 00:24:43,698
If you have anything to teach me,

378
00:24:44,381 --> 00:24:45,451
go right ahead.

379
00:24:57,581 --> 00:24:59,281
What are you looking at?
Can't I take a piss?

380
00:25:00,148 --> 00:25:01,348
Just do your thing.

381
00:25:02,395 --> 00:25:03,895
You can mark your territory
for all I care.

382
00:25:04,554 --> 00:25:05,713
I'm not a dog.

383
00:25:06,110 --> 00:25:07,733
But if I were,

384
00:25:07,758 --> 00:25:09,439
I'd sink my teeth into you
and never let go.

385
00:25:27,306 --> 00:25:28,182
I'll wash mine, too.

386
00:25:29,575 --> 00:25:30,778
Thanks, Mungkorn.

387
00:25:38,791 --> 00:25:39,518
Let's go.

388
00:25:59,351 --> 00:26:01,571
What are you gonna do
about what happened at the karaoke bar?

389
00:26:05,341 --> 00:26:06,868
That was our second kiss, you know.

390
00:26:07,368 --> 00:26:08,674
Can we just be boyfriends already?

391
00:26:10,214 --> 00:26:11,181
You're getting ahead of yourself.

392
00:26:11,794 --> 00:26:13,338
I was just going with the flow.

393
00:26:13,678 --> 00:26:16,081
You were wasted, and that was that.

394
00:26:17,581 --> 00:26:18,781
You're quite something, aren't you?

395
00:26:19,434 --> 00:26:20,797
Playing with my heart, huh?

396
00:26:21,141 --> 00:26:22,311
It is kind of fun.

397
00:26:23,075 --> 00:26:25,571
You play your games, and I'll play mine.

398
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:29,332
As for whether I'm gonna
get serious about you,

399
00:26:30,901 --> 00:26:32,624
only time will tell.

400
00:26:33,194 --> 00:26:35,238
Then I'll keep this up with you.

401
00:26:35,588 --> 00:26:37,078
I can wait.

402
00:26:37,741 --> 00:26:39,605
I've got plenty of patience.

403
00:26:41,567 --> 00:26:43,225
You just keep doing what you're doing,

404
00:26:44,268 --> 00:26:45,842
but I...

405
00:26:46,935 --> 00:26:47,837
play for keeps.

406
00:27:17,661 --> 00:27:20,425
Are you going to tell me
who your boss is?

407
00:27:28,722 --> 00:27:30,189
Just answer the damn question.

408
00:27:30,299 --> 00:27:31,323
You're wasting my time.

409
00:27:31,675 --> 00:27:32,831
Who is your boss?

410
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:38,765
You want me to answer that?

411
00:27:39,733 --> 00:27:41,676
Why don't you give me a massage
like you did that night?

412
00:27:42,330 --> 00:27:43,214
I really liked it.

413
00:27:43,721 --> 00:27:47,831
You know, you two were all over me.

414
00:27:48,269 --> 00:27:49,544
It was such a thrill.

415
00:27:50,698 --> 00:27:53,881
Hey, are you two actually a couple?

416
00:27:59,148 --> 00:28:00,385
That's my business.

417
00:28:00,748 --> 00:28:02,025
Worry about yourself.

418
00:28:02,140 --> 00:28:05,155
Your only job
is to tell me who your boss is.

419
00:28:05,180 --> 00:28:08,508
Well, you two make a fine pair.
You look just like a married couple.

420
00:28:08,532 --> 00:28:09,831
So naturally, I'm curious.

421
00:28:10,248 --> 00:28:11,205
What's wrong with that?

422
00:28:11,761 --> 00:28:12,838
Hey, you.

423
00:28:13,427 --> 00:28:14,417
Have you ever...

424
00:28:16,135 --> 00:28:17,285
gotten a thrill out of him?

425
00:28:20,231 --> 00:28:21,651
F*ck off, you pr*ck.

426
00:28:21,875 --> 00:28:23,478
I ask, you answer.

427
00:28:23,948 --> 00:28:24,905
Simple as that.

428
00:28:25,131 --> 00:28:26,273
You actually startled me.

429
00:28:26,298 --> 00:28:28,200
What do you mean, "f*ck off"?
I'm just telling the truth.

430
00:28:28,225 --> 00:28:30,350
Don't you want him? He's so pretty.
I do want him.

431
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:33,050
With skin that fair
and a face that pretty...

432
00:28:33,075 --> 00:28:36,475
I'd play with him all night long
and nail him in every position.

433
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:39,816
Hell, I'll be the cowboy,
and he can be my rancher.

434
00:28:39,841 --> 00:28:43,538
I'd grab him by the hair.
Then let's take a ride, baby.

435
00:28:43,562 --> 00:28:44,748
"Does it feel good, babe?

436
00:28:44,772 --> 00:28:45,965
Is it nice and tight?"

437
00:28:49,632 --> 00:28:54,029
I'll grind you down, baby,
and say, "Oh, b*tch. That feels good."

438
00:28:54,491 --> 00:28:55,687
"Feels so good, baby.

439
00:28:56,271 --> 00:28:57,868
That's right.

440
00:28:57,892 --> 00:28:59,757
Come on, girl. Come on, come on!"

441
00:29:03,590 --> 00:29:05,743
You piece of sh*t,
show him some respect!

442
00:29:05,768 --> 00:29:07,988
Inspector, please stop!

443
00:29:08,865 --> 00:29:09,846
This is looking bad.

444
00:29:12,933 --> 00:29:15,098
- Inspector!
- Thear, calm down!

445
00:29:15,123 --> 00:29:16,478
Hey, take it easy.

446
00:29:22,091 --> 00:29:23,518
Inspector Thear!

447
00:29:23,687 --> 00:29:25,228
Stop the interrogation immediately.

448
00:29:25,668 --> 00:29:27,051
You're going to get us
into trouble again.

449
00:29:49,008 --> 00:29:50,148
I'm sorry, sir,

450
00:29:50,621 --> 00:29:52,041
for letting my emotions
get the better of me.

451
00:29:54,254 --> 00:29:55,443
It's alright. I understand

452
00:29:56,294 --> 00:29:57,761
that you were
trying to protect your people.

453
00:30:00,521 --> 00:30:02,788
However, you must keep
your personal feelings out of this.

454
00:30:10,554 --> 00:30:12,078
He wants to play chess with him?

455
00:30:12,515 --> 00:30:13,905
Nice move.

456
00:30:16,747 --> 00:30:17,858
Of course.

457
00:30:18,275 --> 00:30:19,871
Told you I'm number one.

458
00:30:20,478 --> 00:30:22,275
I've never lost to anyone.

459
00:30:28,908 --> 00:30:30,198
Didn't you move your knight too far?

460
00:30:32,567 --> 00:30:33,258
Why?

461
00:30:39,141 --> 00:30:40,065
Checkmate.

462
00:30:41,291 --> 00:30:42,115
What the hell?

463
00:30:45,615 --> 00:30:48,031
It's time to keep your promise.

464
00:30:49,660 --> 00:30:51,291
Tell me where your boss is hiding.

465
00:30:52,261 --> 00:30:53,827
Where is he holed up?

466
00:30:55,140 --> 00:30:56,955
Is he still here in Chiang Mai?

467
00:31:32,701 --> 00:31:33,830
It's done, sir.

468
00:31:34,331 --> 00:31:37,072
He said his boss
fled toward Mae Ai last night.

469
00:31:37,522 --> 00:31:39,378
He should be
somewhere in Myanmar by now.

470
00:31:41,975 --> 00:31:42,585
Kanin,

471
00:31:43,518 --> 00:31:45,865
notify the border patrol police
immediately.

472
00:31:46,344 --> 00:31:49,576
Nadol, get in touch
with the Myanmar authorities.

473
00:31:49,601 --> 00:31:52,683
We need to set up an ambush
and bring him in.

474
00:31:52,708 --> 00:31:53,901
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

475
00:32:03,892 --> 00:32:04,566
Thear,

476
00:32:05,398 --> 00:32:06,858
you must have been stressed out lately.

477
00:32:08,320 --> 00:32:10,920
I'll have Saming take over for now.

478
00:32:40,261 --> 00:32:41,628
Whoa.

479
00:32:42,107 --> 00:32:44,052
What was that?
You've never taught me that.

480
00:32:44,345 --> 00:32:46,371
Was that some kind of
advanced interrogation technique?

481
00:32:46,708 --> 00:32:47,912
You want to learn?

482
00:32:49,854 --> 00:32:51,068
So...

483
00:32:51,888 --> 00:32:53,985
what do you have to offer me in return?

484
00:32:54,774 --> 00:32:58,431
You can have whatever you want
as payment for my tuition.

485
00:32:58,456 --> 00:32:59,561
You'd better keep that promise.

486
00:33:00,754 --> 00:33:01,645
Then...

487
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:04,380
you have to have mookrata with me

488
00:33:04,912 --> 00:33:07,167
- Huh?
- so we can spend our time talking.

489
00:33:07,456 --> 00:33:09,040
And if there's anything else
you want to know,

490
00:33:09,180 --> 00:33:10,491
I'll tell you everything.

491
00:33:11,804 --> 00:33:12,748
That's so easy.

492
00:33:13,054 --> 00:33:14,271
Sure thing.

493
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:17,337
I know plenty of great spots.

494
00:33:18,227 --> 00:33:18,871
Belle,

495
00:33:19,667 --> 00:33:21,271
let's go have some mookrata.

496
00:33:21,607 --> 00:33:23,338
I suddenly got a craving for it.

497
00:33:24,067 --> 00:33:25,488
I want the fatty pork.

498
00:33:35,581 --> 00:33:36,528
Thank you.

499
00:33:38,648 --> 00:33:42,024
Saming, what kind of cases
do you like handling?

500
00:33:43,028 --> 00:33:44,228
What kind?

501
00:33:44,545 --> 00:33:46,882
I don't really have
a specific preference.

502
00:33:47,839 --> 00:33:49,941
I just do whatever
the higher-ups order me to do.

503
00:33:50,781 --> 00:33:52,068
As for the Black Bull case,

504
00:33:52,818 --> 00:33:54,128
you took it on yourself, right?

505
00:33:55,065 --> 00:33:57,671
What made you want to handle this case?

506
00:33:59,786 --> 00:34:01,068
Well...

507
00:34:02,093 --> 00:34:03,890
it all started in Phayao.

508
00:34:05,105 --> 00:34:06,241
How should I put it?

509
00:34:07,161 --> 00:34:10,045
Since I was posted to Phayao Station,

510
00:34:10,575 --> 00:34:13,601
I've come to think of Phayao
as my second home.

511
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:17,708
The people there
are nice and kind-hearted.

512
00:34:18,341 --> 00:34:20,278
They've always lived in peace,

513
00:34:21,114 --> 00:34:24,601
but then the Black Bull
started dealing drugs there.

514
00:34:25,495 --> 00:34:27,501
How could I let my home
become a place like that?

515
00:34:27,934 --> 00:34:28,674
Right?

516
00:34:30,441 --> 00:34:32,278
That's such an impressive answer.

517
00:34:35,994 --> 00:34:37,113
So that means...

518
00:34:38,141 --> 00:34:40,771
you've wanted to work on
the Black Bull case all along?

519
00:34:42,808 --> 00:34:43,608
That's right.

520
00:34:44,221 --> 00:34:47,285
My motives aren't as idealistic
as yours, though.

521
00:34:48,021 --> 00:34:49,954
I just thought it was a major case.

522
00:34:50,575 --> 00:34:53,508
If I could be part of this crackdown,

523
00:34:54,581 --> 00:34:56,315
I figured my dream
might finally come true.

524
00:34:57,500 --> 00:34:58,791
What is your dream?

525
00:34:59,927 --> 00:35:00,878
Well...

526
00:35:02,948 --> 00:35:03,870
To get rich,

527
00:35:04,838 --> 00:35:05,959
to get promoted,

528
00:35:07,728 --> 00:35:10,208
and to save enough
to buy my mom a house. That's it.

529
00:35:22,041 --> 00:35:24,339
If I could make your dream come true,

530
00:35:24,855 --> 00:35:26,638
I'd do whatever it takes.

531
00:35:30,893 --> 00:35:32,557
Thank you, Saming.

532
00:35:33,814 --> 00:35:35,791
But to be honest with you,

533
00:35:36,853 --> 00:35:40,488
talent and effort alone aren't enough.

534
00:35:41,168 --> 00:35:45,258
I had to use a few tricks
to get to where I am today.

535
00:35:47,346 --> 00:35:48,411
What kind of trick?

536
00:35:50,221 --> 00:35:52,221
I might tell you...

537
00:35:52,873 --> 00:35:54,120
on our next date.

538
00:35:59,448 --> 00:36:00,678
Keep your promise, though.

539
00:36:01,021 --> 00:36:02,545
I always keep my promises.

540
00:36:06,467 --> 00:36:10,251
Hey, you're so busy flirting.
The pork's burning. Flip it already!

541
00:36:11,141 --> 00:36:12,224
What are you doing here?

542
00:36:13,215 --> 00:36:14,223
Move over.

543
00:36:14,926 --> 00:36:15,651
Hey!

544
00:36:16,334 --> 00:36:17,239
Scoot over.

545
00:36:17,564 --> 00:36:18,508
Hey, make some room.

546
00:36:18,532 --> 00:36:20,075
Belle, sit right here.

547
00:36:21,922 --> 00:36:24,325
This is my favorite mookrata place.

548
00:36:24,971 --> 00:36:27,760
I love the food here,
so I wanted Belle to try it.

549
00:36:28,641 --> 00:36:30,409
Thear said the dipping sauce here
is to die for,

550
00:36:30,434 --> 00:36:31,940
so I wanted to give it a try.

551
00:36:33,512 --> 00:36:34,588
Hello, Belle.

552
00:36:34,612 --> 00:36:37,417
I'm Saming, Thear's old friend.

553
00:36:37,631 --> 00:36:39,708
Hello, Saming.

554
00:36:39,732 --> 00:36:41,343
You never told me about him.

555
00:36:41,368 --> 00:36:43,362
I mean, I'd completely
forgotten he existed.

556
00:36:44,301 --> 00:36:45,741
I only remembered when I saw him.

557
00:36:45,850 --> 00:36:47,699
We used to be really close.

558
00:36:47,724 --> 00:36:49,308
I'd love to take a trip
down memory lane.

559
00:36:49,616 --> 00:36:51,494
Let's just eat with them.

560
00:36:52,220 --> 00:36:53,513
Here, your plate.

561
00:36:54,573 --> 00:36:56,347
The pork's all burnt.
It's bad, you know.

562
00:36:58,701 --> 00:37:01,233
Excuse me, can we have two more sets?

563
00:37:01,710 --> 00:37:03,585
My old friend and I
are having a reunion.

564
00:37:03,684 --> 00:37:06,314
Bring me two glasses of beer, too.

565
00:37:06,848 --> 00:37:08,167
Oops!

566
00:37:08,741 --> 00:37:11,001
I hope I'm not
interrupting your private time.

567
00:37:11,319 --> 00:37:12,608
Were you having
a private conversation?

568
00:37:13,575 --> 00:37:14,701
Kind of.

569
00:37:15,241 --> 00:37:17,374
There are things
we'd rather keep private, though.

570
00:37:19,574 --> 00:37:21,029
Keeping secrets, are we?

571
00:37:21,054 --> 00:37:23,450
Just make sure
you don't leak any classified info.

572
00:37:23,475 --> 00:37:24,441
That's a serious offense.

573
00:37:25,023 --> 00:37:27,543
I know what I should and shouldn't do.

574
00:37:27,794 --> 00:37:30,850
No baseless claims,
and no abuse of power.

575
00:37:31,814 --> 00:37:33,197
Good. That's great.

576
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:34,900
At least you know
the police code of ethics.

577
00:37:35,080 --> 00:37:37,322
Let me give you
one more piece of advice, though.

578
00:37:38,113 --> 00:37:40,730
Learn to read people better

579
00:37:41,774 --> 00:37:43,214
before you end up as someone's prey.

580
00:37:43,767 --> 00:37:45,228
You don't need to lecture him.

581
00:37:45,530 --> 00:37:46,898
He knows what's right and wrong

582
00:37:47,541 --> 00:37:49,425
and what's best for himself.

583
00:37:50,198 --> 00:37:51,418
Right, Mungkorn?

584
00:37:51,675 --> 00:37:52,971
That's right, Saming.

585
00:37:53,141 --> 00:37:55,108
See? That's good, too.

586
00:37:55,627 --> 00:37:56,844
That's how I trained you.

587
00:38:05,541 --> 00:38:09,828
- Bottoms up!
- Bottoms up!

588
00:38:12,814 --> 00:38:13,628
Are you okay?

589
00:38:13,670 --> 00:38:14,820
There's still some left.

590
00:38:15,491 --> 00:38:17,384
All talk, huh?

591
00:38:17,533 --> 00:38:20,759
- Thought you could hold your liquor.
- I'm just going easy on you.

592
00:38:20,784 --> 00:38:22,651
- Wow.
- I didn't want you to look bad.

593
00:38:22,676 --> 00:38:24,188
Stop trying to sound cool.

594
00:38:24,212 --> 00:38:26,918
Just admit you're a lightweight.

595
00:38:27,375 --> 00:38:29,081
- You calling me a lightweight?
- Yeah.

596
00:38:29,423 --> 00:38:31,111
How about we settle this
with our fists, you bastard?

597
00:38:31,136 --> 00:38:32,488
You bet.

598
00:38:32,513 --> 00:38:34,191
You always take
what belongs to someone else.

599
00:38:34,216 --> 00:38:35,508
What the hell are you talking about?

600
00:38:35,533 --> 00:38:36,808
- You want to fight me?
- Bring it on.

601
00:38:36,833 --> 00:38:38,456
- What are you rambling about?
- Come on.

602
00:38:38,481 --> 00:38:39,986
- What's your f*cking problem?
- Oh, you wanna fight?

603
00:38:40,264 --> 00:38:41,904
- What's your problem?
- Come on, hit me.

604
00:38:41,928 --> 00:38:43,704
Jeez, enough already!

605
00:38:45,064 --> 00:38:46,958
You're both drunk.
Just go home already.

606
00:38:47,533 --> 00:38:49,068
You're both high-ranking officers.

607
00:38:49,093 --> 00:38:50,760
Have some shame. You're in public.

608
00:38:57,504 --> 00:39:00,497
Belle, please drive
Inspector Thear home.

609
00:39:00,941 --> 00:39:02,474
I don't know how to drive.

610
00:39:03,704 --> 00:39:05,530
He wouldn't be able to drive, either.

611
00:39:05,555 --> 00:39:06,588
Hey, I'm fine.

612
00:39:06,612 --> 00:39:08,395
My house is right here.
I'll just...

613
00:39:09,805 --> 00:39:12,391
Listen to yourself!
I don't wanna die in Thailand.

614
00:39:16,741 --> 00:39:18,191
I'll give him a ride, then.

615
00:39:21,550 --> 00:39:22,668
Saming,

616
00:39:22,891 --> 00:39:25,058
I'll take Inspector Thear home.

617
00:39:25,341 --> 00:39:26,488
Is that okay?

618
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:27,747
That's fine.

619
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:30,607
You should take him home.

620
00:39:31,473 --> 00:39:33,806
I was just joking.
Didn't think he'd take it seriously.

621
00:39:36,508 --> 00:39:38,085
We'll talk later, then.

622
00:39:38,898 --> 00:39:40,951
Make sure you get home safe, alright?

623
00:39:41,241 --> 00:39:42,498
Drive safe.

624
00:39:42,563 --> 00:39:43,936
Okay. See you later.

625
00:39:44,052 --> 00:39:44,857
See you.

626
00:39:49,547 --> 00:39:50,597
Let's go, Belle.

627
00:39:51,241 --> 00:39:52,431
See you later.

628
00:39:53,922 --> 00:39:55,227
How are you getting back?

629
00:39:56,111 --> 00:39:57,778
- Have some shame, Inspector.
- You can't drive while you're drunk!

630
00:39:57,984 --> 00:39:59,758
Or you're gonna get arrested!

631
00:40:00,261 --> 00:40:01,768
Just get your ass home already.

632
00:40:07,217 --> 00:40:09,871
This is all your fault.
Look what you've done to me.

633
00:40:10,541 --> 00:40:13,809
It's not very nice of you
to make me fall and treat me like this.

634
00:40:13,834 --> 00:40:14,638
Inspector.

635
00:40:14,778 --> 00:40:16,040
You're going to hell

636
00:40:16,065 --> 00:40:18,497
- for hurting an old man.
- You're drunk and not making any sense.

637
00:40:19,103 --> 00:40:21,816
- Dammit, I'm old, you know.
- Just stop talking.

638
00:40:21,841 --> 00:40:22,907
Get in the car.

639
00:40:22,932 --> 00:40:24,408
- A Northern guy has feelings...
- Ugh!

640
00:40:25,031 --> 00:40:26,981
I'm so fed up with both of you.

641
00:40:29,254 --> 00:40:30,821
I'm just going to tell him, Thear.

642
00:40:32,708 --> 00:40:35,158
He called me here
just to make you jealous.

643
00:40:38,732 --> 00:40:39,478
What?

644
00:40:40,681 --> 00:40:44,164
Didn't he say he was going to marry you?

645
00:40:45,513 --> 00:40:47,423
It was all just part of his plan.

646
00:40:48,584 --> 00:40:50,508
Ever since you two got married,

647
00:40:50,532 --> 00:40:52,266
you've had nothing but bad luck, right?

648
00:40:52,354 --> 00:40:53,971
That's why he called me.

649
00:40:54,080 --> 00:40:56,656
You'd hate him,
and the curse would finally break.

650
00:40:58,795 --> 00:41:01,424
Belle is lying through her teeth.

651
00:41:02,117 --> 00:41:02,948
Nonsense.

652
00:41:04,119 --> 00:41:04,924
Don't listen to her.

653
00:41:09,084 --> 00:41:11,028
So the reason for my bad luck was...

654
00:41:15,677 --> 00:41:17,240
Why didn't you tell me, Inspector?

655
00:41:23,098 --> 00:41:26,883
He knew that if he did,
you'd never stop loving him.

656
00:41:27,654 --> 00:41:29,548
And he couldn't stand seeing you hurt,

657
00:41:29,572 --> 00:41:30,931
so he chose to take the pain himself.

658
00:41:32,915 --> 00:41:34,308
That's enough.
What are you talking about?

659
00:41:34,332 --> 00:41:36,676
That's not true at all.
I'm too tired to keep correcting you.

660
00:41:38,548 --> 00:41:39,708
But what you're doing...

661
00:41:40,379 --> 00:41:41,514
hurts me, too.

662
00:41:42,715 --> 00:41:45,059
What are you so hurt about?

663
00:41:45,528 --> 00:41:47,256
You're into Saming, aren't you?

664
00:41:47,304 --> 00:41:50,268
You even said
I was some cheap knockoff of a husband.

665
00:41:50,292 --> 00:41:51,991
So why are you acting like the victim?

666
00:41:52,461 --> 00:41:54,094
I'm not into Saming.

667
00:41:56,513 --> 00:41:58,241
I'm in the middle of a mission.

668
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:01,678
What kind of mission?
Can I hear about it, too?

669
00:42:06,901 --> 00:42:08,217
A guy like that

670
00:42:08,878 --> 00:42:10,571
isn't worth your love.

671
00:42:10,908 --> 00:42:12,616
You deserve someone better.

672
00:42:12,717 --> 00:42:13,713
If it were me,

673
00:42:14,619 --> 00:42:16,617
I would never hurt you.

674
00:42:17,107 --> 00:42:19,900
I'd never let you be just a rebound

675
00:42:20,377 --> 00:42:22,260
while waiting for an ex to come back.

676
00:42:22,294 --> 00:42:25,025
(Saming seems to know a lot about me,)

677
00:42:25,050 --> 00:42:27,403
(from personal stuff
to cases I've never told him about.)

678
00:42:27,428 --> 00:42:29,203
(Nadol: The raid failed. It was a trap.)
It's a message from the group chat.

679
00:42:29,228 --> 00:42:33,067
It says the raid mission failed.

680
00:42:33,126 --> 00:42:34,497
They were caught in a trap.

681
00:42:35,399 --> 00:42:37,212
The Black Bull...

682
00:42:37,727 --> 00:42:39,564
won't let themselves be caught easily.

683
00:42:40,460 --> 00:42:41,807
The only way to catch them

684
00:42:42,128 --> 00:42:44,307
is when they actually want to be caught.

685
00:42:44,777 --> 00:42:47,627
I suspect that Saming is a mole
working for the Black Bull.

686
00:42:49,214 --> 00:42:50,708
So that means...

687
00:42:51,397 --> 00:42:53,243
you both still love each other.

688
00:42:54,024 --> 00:42:57,108
It's just that
one is too focused on work,

689
00:42:57,265 --> 00:43:00,828
while the other
is trying too hard to be the good guy.

690
00:43:05,925 --> 00:43:07,392
You were so busy
acting like the good guy.

691
00:43:08,147 --> 00:43:10,837
If I hadn't learned the truth,
you would've ended up being the bad guy.

692
00:43:13,175 --> 00:43:16,861
I just wanted you to be safe.
That's all there is to it.

693
00:43:17,688 --> 00:43:18,708
I know,

694
00:43:19,530 --> 00:43:20,960
but don't ever do that again.

695
00:43:22,194 --> 00:43:25,616
Physical pain is one thing,
but a broken heart is harder to heal.

696
00:43:41,544 --> 00:43:44,478
Jeez, Inspector.
You just threw up.

697
00:43:45,877 --> 00:43:46,930
That's gross.

698
00:43:47,906 --> 00:43:49,548
Yeah, you're right.

699
00:43:50,209 --> 00:43:51,069
My bad.

700
00:43:52,007 --> 00:43:53,123
I'll give you a hug, then.

701
00:44:35,485 --> 00:44:37,982
Why do you always have to
make things so complicated?

702
00:44:38,475 --> 00:44:39,896
Well, I didn't know.

703
00:44:41,083 --> 00:44:42,623
I didn't know what else to do.

704
00:44:44,454 --> 00:44:47,378
I didn't want you
to take the fall for me.

705
00:44:49,108 --> 00:44:50,598
You were so busy playing the good guy

706
00:44:51,901 --> 00:44:53,498
that you didn't think about my feelings.

707
00:44:55,634 --> 00:44:57,257
I feel bad for Belle, too,

708
00:44:57,574 --> 00:44:59,311
having to put on an act with you.

709
00:45:00,875 --> 00:45:02,991
Sometimes I wanna give you
a good smack.

710
00:45:03,678 --> 00:45:05,071
Hit me, then.

711
00:45:05,987 --> 00:45:07,330
I can handle the pain,

712
00:45:08,280 --> 00:45:10,271
but I won't let anything happen to you.

713
00:45:12,854 --> 00:45:14,118
You're doing it again.

714
00:45:15,648 --> 00:45:18,565
If we touch each other
or show any affection,

715
00:45:19,328 --> 00:45:20,738
will it hurt me?

716
00:45:22,574 --> 00:45:23,289
Yes.

717
00:45:25,247 --> 00:45:27,367
We're not doing anything together

718
00:45:29,437 --> 00:45:31,884
until I figure out how to fix this.

719
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:37,005
Jeez, then what are we supposed to do?

720
00:45:37,322 --> 00:45:39,331
We're sleeping in the same bed,
but we can't do a thing.

721
00:45:40,075 --> 00:45:41,231
It's driving me crazy.

722
00:45:41,475 --> 00:45:43,018
Yeah, I know.

723
00:45:43,556 --> 00:45:45,384
I'm barely holding myself back, too.

724
00:46:05,915 --> 00:46:07,063
How about this?

725
00:46:07,585 --> 00:46:11,641
We can hug and kiss through this bear.

726
00:46:13,108 --> 00:46:16,591
Maybe it'll ease
the bad luck and the pain.

727
00:46:20,302 --> 00:46:21,515
Are you serious?

728
00:46:23,908 --> 00:46:25,044
Just do it.

729
00:46:26,248 --> 00:46:29,271
I don't think
the heaven and earth are that strict.

730
00:46:36,414 --> 00:46:37,884
Fine, let's do it.

731
00:46:53,243 --> 00:46:58,190
♪That level of cuteness
is against the law♪

732
00:46:58,215 --> 00:47:03,116
♪I must be under your spell,
can I blame you at all?♪

733
00:47:03,141 --> 00:47:05,530
♪You're guilty
of messing with my heart,♪

734
00:47:05,556 --> 00:47:08,009
♪Stirring up my feelings
right from the start,♪

735
00:47:08,041 --> 00:47:11,431
♪The fine you'll pay
is your whole heart♪

736
00:47:11,456 --> 00:47:15,750
♪You take the blame,
I'll take the love part♪

737
00:47:16,990 --> 00:47:18,866
♪Your smile should be under arrest♪

738
00:47:19,318 --> 00:47:20,466
That feels a bit better.

739
00:47:21,812 --> 00:47:23,922
♪Stop! Hands on your head, honey♪

740
00:47:23,947 --> 00:47:26,723
♪You've got quite a few charges, baby,♪

741
00:47:26,748 --> 00:47:31,743
♪For trespassing
on my heart deliberately,♪

742
00:47:31,768 --> 00:47:33,793
♪So there'll be no bail or parole♪

743
00:47:33,818 --> 00:47:38,286
♪'Cause your heart is under my control♪

744
00:47:38,311 --> 00:47:40,823
♪With all the evidence I have found,♪

745
00:47:40,848 --> 00:47:44,723
♪Guess I'll have to
take you into custody now♪

746
00:47:44,748 --> 00:47:49,536
♪That level of cuteness
is against the law♪

747
00:47:49,658 --> 00:47:54,330
♪I must be under your spell,
can I blame you at all?♪

748
00:47:54,534 --> 00:47:57,088
♪You're guilty
of messing with my heart,♪

749
00:47:57,120 --> 00:47:58,901
♪Stirring up my feelings
right from the start♪

750
00:48:00,190 --> 00:48:01,838
If you can't even control your own body,

751
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,391
then what the hell are you good for?

752
00:48:03,416 --> 00:48:04,422
As police officers,

753
00:48:04,713 --> 00:48:06,940
are we forbidden from yawning
or feeling sleepy?

754
00:48:07,487 --> 00:48:08,648
Are you talking back to me?

755
00:48:10,463 --> 00:48:12,252
I told you I'd take care
of this one myself.

756
00:48:12,277 --> 00:48:13,642
So why the hell are you trying
to steal him from me?

757
00:48:13,667 --> 00:48:15,502
I keep telling you,
I haven't done anything.

758
00:48:15,527 --> 00:48:16,174
You bastard!

759
00:48:16,869 --> 00:48:17,814
What's going on?

760
00:48:23,369 --> 00:48:28,303
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

761
00:48:28,330 --> 00:48:33,103
♪But the more I run,
the more you're on my mind♪

762
00:48:33,128 --> 00:48:37,364
♪If you're gonna love me,
don't break the deal we made♪

763
00:48:37,389 --> 00:48:42,884
♪Don't break my heart,
remember what you said?♪

764
00:48:42,909 --> 00:48:47,897
♪Let's call off the deal
and let our hearts decide♪

765
00:48:47,922 --> 00:48:54,277
♪From contracting parties to lovers,
does that sound alright?♪

766
00:49:00,572 --> 00:49:03,810
♪It's time you became mine♪
